1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:01,870
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,640
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,510
(Episode 31)

5
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:14,790
Darn.

6
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:18,490
Darn mosquitoes are everywhere.

7
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:30,540
- Hey, you can sit here.
- Oh, thank you.

8
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,980
Here, there is this thing
called a lodging fee.

9
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,150
How much is it?

10
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,010
Do I really have
to spell it out for you?

11
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,420
Show some sincerity and pay up.

12
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,090
Here.

13
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:57,300
Are you kidding me?

14
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,660
This is the best spot
to beat the heat.

15
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:01,770
It should be at least three bills.

16
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,740
Three bills? As in three dollars?

17
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,240
Forget it.

18
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:07,770
What are you, a beggar?

19
00:01:08,570 --> 00:01:11,140
- Get lost.
- Then give me my money back.

20
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:12,540
I won't sit here.

21
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:15,250
Why you... Get lost.

22
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,380
Give it back.

23
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:17,480
Get lost, darn it!

24
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,250
But...

25
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:21,990
Unbelievable.

26
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:33,130
I still don't get it.

27
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:35,130
I'm the only one
with a mosquito allergy.

28
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:38,370
Everyone's built differently.

29
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:40,040
Allergies aren't always shared
across a family.

30
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:43,010
It's strange, though.

31
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,480
Built differently or not,

32
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,080
I honestly feel like I don't take
after either Mom or Dad.

33
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:51,480
Isn't it normal to take after
at least one side of your family?

34
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:53,220
You do.

35
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:56,220
In what way?
How do I take after them?

36
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:59,390
The CEO and the Chairman
are both quite tall.

37
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,390
That's why you're on
the taller side.

38
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:03,730
Is that so?

39
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:07,730
I suppose I'm pretty tall
thanks to Mom and Dad.

40
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:09,230
Try not to scratch too much.

41
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:12,970
If you can just get through tonight,
it won't blister.

42
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,110
Okay. Thank you, Ms. Joo.

43
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:39,700
(Year 1988)

44
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,240
(Joo Ae Sook)

45
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,380
Thank you.

46
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:57,780
Did you get the medicine for me?

47
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:02,050
Yes, you always seem
to be looking for it.

48
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:06,190
(An Guk Cheol)

49
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:09,660
Thank you, Ae Sook.

50
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:20,610
(Labor Cost Calculation Table)

51
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,480
(Don't skimp on it
and apply generously.)

52
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:31,780
(I'll gladly get you some more.)

53
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,420
Don't skimp on it
and apply generously.

54
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,220
I'll gladly get you some more.

55
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,260
Here we go.

56
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:47,200
Is anyone going to hit the jackpot?

57
00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:49,630
All right.

58
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,740
All right, I call.

59
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:56,570
- You're going to match that?
- Sounds good.

60
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,580
This is what you should've matched.

61
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,610
You're all in?

62
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,250
Let's see what you have.

63
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:05,420
- I have a nine.
- A nine it is.

64
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:07,990
Do not even try,
I have a pair of twos.

65
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:09,550
Hold it.

66
00:04:11,090 --> 00:04:12,390
Pair of tens.

67
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,660
How much is all this?

68
00:04:26,170 --> 00:04:27,170
Hey.

69
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,370
- What? What is it?
- Hey!

70
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:31,940
Isn't that your wife?

71
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,080
Has she lost her mind coming here?

72
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,850
Joo Ae Sook,
are you out of your mind?

73
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:40,490
Well, I was just worried
you'd lose all our money again.

74
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,590
I swear, I'll...

75
00:04:42,650 --> 00:04:43,690
Follow me.

76
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,320
Come on, darn it!

77
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:52,230
No wonder I had terrible luck today.

78
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,500
You're like a curse, aren't you?

79
00:04:55,230 --> 00:04:56,530
Didn't I tell you not to come?

80
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:59,000
Are my words a joke?
Is your husband a joke to you?

81
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,840
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

82
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:06,410
But that money is all we have left.

83
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:08,810
We have to pay off our debt with it.

84
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,120
That's why your husband...

85
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,580
is trying to double or triple it.

86
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:15,090
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

87
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,120
It's all my fault.

88
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,490
A woman should just stay home
and wait.

89
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:21,060
With you out and about,
nothing can go right.

90
00:05:28,930 --> 00:05:31,240
You're so cold-hearted,
you won't even let out a groan.

91
00:06:40,710 --> 00:06:43,140
(Your Skin Becomes More Beautiful,
Like the Morning Sun)

92
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:44,540
(Actress Kim Jung Sun)

93
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,710
It's all your fault.

94
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:51,680
It's all your fault!

95
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:57,960
It's all your fault!

96
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:09,170
(Actress Kim Jung Sun)

97
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:20,110
Dr. Ji Seong Jun, 2,240.

98
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:23,010
Dr. Ji Seong Jun, 2,240.

99
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:26,980
Excuse me, young lady.

100
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:32,220
I'm saying this
because it hits close to home.

101
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:35,990
Don't live like that.
Just run away or something.

102
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:38,660
I can tell you're still young.

103
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:41,430
Why stay with a guy
who beats you up?

104
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:46,940
Leave without any regrets
while you're still childless.

105
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:48,810
Got it?

106
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:58,550
Will the guardian
for patient Kim Min Jeong in Ward 62...

107
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:00,480
please come to the room?

108
00:08:00,550 --> 00:08:03,650
Will the guardian
for patient Kim Min Jeong in Ward 62...

109
00:08:03,690 --> 00:08:05,620
please come to the room?

110
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:09,660
(Women's Life, Kim Jung Sun)

111
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:19,170
What are you doing?

112
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,350
(Actress Kim Jung Sun,
Daughter of Cheongma,)

113
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,880
(Gets Engaged to Elite Talent
Kang Young Hoon)

114
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,450
What you took from me,

115
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:37,560
I'll get it back.

116
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:41,930
Just wait, Kim Jung Sun.

117
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,010
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

118
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:04,350
More than anything,
I think we need to figure out...

119
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,420
where the board members stand first.

120
00:09:06,950 --> 00:09:08,990
Given the nature of the business,

121
00:09:09,050 --> 00:09:11,490
a lot of people
will probably be against it.

122
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:15,190
Please look closely into
where the board members stand.

123
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:20,230
Director Joo?

124
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:24,870
What? Oh, yes, I'll get on it.

125
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:28,470
I'll even find out
their political leanings.

126
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:29,840
Right, thanks for that.

127
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:34,880
That reminds me.
You hired a new secretary.

128
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:36,550
Yes.

129
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:39,050
I hired him in a hurry,
but he seems quite smart.

130
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:40,990
That's a relief.

131
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:44,620
You certainly have an eye
for people.

132
00:09:45,490 --> 00:09:49,790
That's why I rely on you so much.

133
00:09:52,230 --> 00:09:53,400
Thank you, ma'am.

134
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:56,870
Nicely done.

135
00:09:57,970 --> 00:10:01,940
The design silhouette is important,
but what matters most is the fit.

136
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:03,810
Let's thoroughly test everything,

137
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:05,310
including
the extra reinforced leather.

138
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,580
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

139
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:12,050
Wait, Ms. Kang.
Is that a matching ring?

140
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:14,750
Yes, we just got them.

141
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:17,990
Chief, I see
you're not wearing yours.

142
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:27,570
You must have taken it off
for the factory inspection this morning.

143
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:31,000
That's a wrap for today's meeting.

144
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,200
Yes, sir.

145
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,380
Seriously.
Why did you take off your ring?

146
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:44,420
Didn't you hear?
I went to the factory this morning.

147
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:46,220
Why can't you wear it
at the factory?

148
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,120
Do you operate
the machines yourself?

149
00:10:49,990 --> 00:10:51,090
Kang Hae Ra.

150
00:10:51,390 --> 00:10:53,290
We don't need
to make it obvious at work.

151
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:55,760
If you want the CEO to notice,

152
00:10:55,830 --> 00:10:57,760
I can wear them
in front of your parents.

153
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,500
You'll take it on and off?
Are you kidding me right now?

154
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:02,330
We're at the office.

155
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:05,400
I don't want to bring
personal matters into our work.

156
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:10,140
Be honest with me.

157
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:11,640
About what?

158
00:11:11,710 --> 00:11:12,810
It's because of Ko Eun Seol, right?

159
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:15,250
Is Ko Eun Seol the reason
you're not wearing it?

160
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:17,780
She likes you,
and that's been affecting you.

161
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:21,420
You're right.

162
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,890
- She's getting to me.
- Seok Jin.

163
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,060
But even if she gets to me,

164
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:29,660
it's nothing compared to
how much I want to marry you.

165
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:35,070
Still, you took it off
because of her.

166
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:37,070
Wearing matching rings with you...

167
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:39,200
makes me feel
like an incompetent person...

168
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:40,770
who only landed this job
with the CEO's backing.

169
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:43,040
But that's not the case.

170
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:46,110
Why do you have
to twist things like that?

171
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:47,750
That's how I feel.

172
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:50,550
So please try to understand
my position.

173
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:55,650
Fine, whatever.

174
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:58,090
If it bothers you that much,
just wear it around Dad.

175
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,760
But why do you have to be
so unnecessarily honest?

176
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:05,000
You told me to be honest.

177
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:10,530
Let's grab some lunch.
What should we eat? Let's go.

178
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:12,640
Come on.

179
00:12:15,170 --> 00:12:17,270
Did the new employee orientation
go well?

180
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,880
Yes, I'm up to speed
on secretarial support too.

181
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,150
Secretary Choi, from now on,

182
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:28,590
your duties will differ
from typical secretarial work.

183
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,260
Yes, as an executive secretary,

184
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:34,130
I understand my duty is
to provide close support to you.

185
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:35,690
Close support?

186
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,190
There's a nice ring to it.

187
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,900
In that sense,

188
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:45,070
there must be absolutely no secrets
between you and me.

189
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,740
Of course,
whatever happens between us...

190
00:12:48,010 --> 00:12:49,670
has to stay strictly confidential.

191
00:12:52,810 --> 00:12:54,980
The Cheongma Scholarship Foundation
is starting...

192
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:56,680
a new prison scholarship program.

193
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,920
It hasn't even begun,
but people are already talking.

194
00:13:00,380 --> 00:13:03,520
It's a scholarship program
for inmates, you see.

195
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:09,390
We'll need to figure out in advance
how this will benefit or harm...

196
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,460
Cheongma Group, right?

197
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,800
Sure, I'll look into it closely.

198
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:17,840
Good.

199
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:20,240
Any Cheongma Group employee
should do that.

200
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,540
However,

201
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:24,780
Secretary Choi,
you need to be different.

202
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:28,950
Rather than the company's
profits and losses,

203
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:33,020
you must only think about
what benefits and harms me.

204
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,090
Have I made myself clear?

205
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,990
Yes. If I can be of assistance,

206
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,460
I'll do everything I can.

207
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,400
Without you,

208
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,700
I'd probably still be...

209
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:50,270
shaking kids down for money
in back alleys.

210
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:53,900
To be able to repay
your kindness like this...

211
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,470
is truly an honor.

212
00:14:02,150 --> 00:14:03,210
So...

213
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:07,950
Are you saying I should contact
this number from now on?

214
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:09,520
Yes.

215
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:13,220
From now on, all contact with her
goes through me.

216
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,430
Well,

217
00:14:14,890 --> 00:14:16,830
are you her new servant
or something?

218
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,200
I am her executive secretary,
Choi Jun Hwan.

219
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,530
Okay, I got it. I'll do as told.

220
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,640
Have you figured out
An Guk Cheol's movements?

221
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:27,370
There's nothing to report.

222
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,010
He just hangs
around Jisan Station...

223
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:32,580
and hits up the soup kitchen
at mealtime.

224
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,380
That's basically the gist of it.

225
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:39,150
What kind of lavish schedule
would a homeless guy even have?

226
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,520
By the way,

227
00:14:42,550 --> 00:14:44,120
what kind of life
did Ms. Joo have...

228
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,390
to end up getting involved...

229
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:49,930
with a piece of trash like him?

230
00:14:50,130 --> 00:14:51,600
As her servant...

231
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:54,100
I mean, as her executive secretary,

232
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:55,470
you would know.

233
00:14:55,570 --> 00:14:58,840
You will not ask
any personal questions...

234
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:01,240
regarding Director Joo.

235
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:08,180
If you snoop around the Director
out of unnecessary curiosity...

236
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:12,180
this place will be
completely cleared out,

237
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:14,080
including you.

238
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:20,760
Where are you going?

239
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,460
I'm off to my driving gig.

240
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,190
They pop up occasionally
during the day.

241
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:25,760
Sit here before you go.

242
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:27,770
What for?

243
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:35,310
You went to where
Eun Seol's biological mother lives.

244
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:39,310
How are her living conditions?
I bet she's dirt poor.

245
00:15:41,150 --> 00:15:42,150
Not really.

246
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:45,380
No? Then is she well-off?

247
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:48,690
Well, it's not that either.

248
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,960
Just out with it, you punk.
Is she rich or poor?

249
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:58,660
She's no longer in this world.
She passed away three years ago.

250
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,330
- She died?
- That's why...

251
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,570
you can't say a word to Eun Seol.

252
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:07,840
It seems like
she had a rough life...

253
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:10,610
since debt collectors are
still coming after her.

254
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:12,810
Debt collectors?

255
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,950
If those debt collectors
find out about Eun Seol,

256
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:20,050
they will come running
and try to collect that debt.

257
00:16:20,550 --> 00:16:23,420
So, you must never
tell Eun Seol, okay?

258
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:27,830
Unbelievable.
Talk about a cursed kid.

259
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:30,730
The mother who raised her
died horribly,

260
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:33,660
and her biological mother
had a rough life too?

261
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:36,770
Of all the babies,

262
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:39,540
did your wife have to bring home one
that's cursed?

263
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,840
Oh, my.

264
00:16:42,570 --> 00:16:45,910
I'm going to say something
to Eun Seol just in case.

265
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:48,450
She should focus
on her job right now,

266
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:51,780
and not think about
finding her mother for a while.

267
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:55,520
So you need to keep
your mouth shut too. Got it?

268
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,790
Do you expect me to do it for free?

269
00:16:58,660 --> 00:16:59,890
Are you kidding me?

270
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:08,130
- Okay, 200 dollars.
- Make that 250.

271
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,270
Eun Seol?

272
00:17:14,910 --> 00:17:16,370
Do you have a lot of work left?

273
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,740
No, once I finish this, I'm done.

274
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,680
Let's get off work together then.

275
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,150
Sounds good. Just a moment.

276
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:29,990
What's that?

277
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:34,320
It's a gift for the person
I'm meeting tomorrow.

278
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:38,960
Would it be too much
if I asked who it is?

279
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:43,300
It's Chief Cha's mother.

280
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,200
Chief Cha's mother?

281
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,400
Yes.

282
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:50,770
I helped her a while ago,

283
00:17:51,140 --> 00:17:53,780
and she really wants to see me.

284
00:17:54,950 --> 00:17:57,110
Right, I see.

285
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,020
Eun Seol,

286
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,790
by any chance,

287
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,690
do you still have feelings
for Chief Cha?

288
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,860
Excuse me?

289
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,600
I'm worried, that's all.

290
00:18:14,530 --> 00:18:18,140
Chief Cha is engaged to Ms. Kang.

291
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:21,610
And Ms. Kang is the daughter
of the owner of Cheongma Group.

292
00:18:23,810 --> 00:18:25,780
If this is just a passing phase,

293
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,510
you've got way too much to lose.

294
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:32,680
Right.

295
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:35,820
My first and foremost priority...

296
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:39,590
is making sure
you don't get hurt anymore.

297
00:18:44,230 --> 00:18:46,300
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

298
00:18:49,270 --> 00:18:51,370
- I'm home.
- Hey.

299
00:18:51,970 --> 00:18:53,640
Come and have a seat.

300
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:02,980
So, is everything okay at work?

301
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:04,780
What?

302
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:06,650
Did any of your superiors...

303
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:09,420
say anything strange to you?

304
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,960
My superior?

305
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,320
Nothing like that happened.

306
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:15,630
Oh, really?

307
00:19:16,690 --> 00:19:20,860
Well, you know, you...

308
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,580
Never mind.

309
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:35,250
Just watch out
for the people closest to you.

310
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:39,120
No matter how close you are
to people at work,

311
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:42,250
they're always the ones
who stab you in the back.

312
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:48,260
Sure thing. Don't worry, Grandma.

313
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:50,860
- I'll go change.
- Sure.

314
00:19:56,830 --> 00:19:57,830
Unbelievable.

315
00:20:05,710 --> 00:20:06,710
Are you working?

316
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,280
Hey.

317
00:20:12,950 --> 00:20:14,220
Drink this while you work.

318
00:20:15,690 --> 00:20:17,390
- Thanks, Dad.
- Sure.

319
00:20:23,230 --> 00:20:25,560
Did you have something to say?

320
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:28,930
What? Well, it's nothing important.

321
00:20:30,570 --> 00:20:32,140
Are you enjoying work?

322
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:36,570
Yes. Your daughter gets praised
so much at work.

323
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:40,380
Good.
There's the Ko Eun Seol I know.

324
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,850
Lately, maybe because
you're more at ease,

325
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:45,980
your face looks much brighter.

326
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,920
You even look prettier.

327
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,260
- Really?
- Yes.

328
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:55,430
So, just enjoy it for a while.

329
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:57,190
What?

330
00:20:57,190 --> 00:20:59,860
Go on dates you missed out on, okay?

331
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:02,670
Enjoy your work like you do now
and do your best.

332
00:21:02,770 --> 00:21:06,600
Just focus entirely on yourself.

333
00:21:08,070 --> 00:21:11,240
Put the thought of finding
your birth mother...

334
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,180
aside for a moment, okay?

335
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:19,850
You must've been upset that I wanted
to look for my biological mother.

336
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:21,020
Gosh, no.

337
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,950
I didn't mean it like that.

338
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,790
I think you did.

339
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:26,820
You were a little upset.

340
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:30,130
Well, maybe a little bit.

341
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,570
- Dad.
- Yes?

342
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:40,500
No matter what anyone says,

343
00:21:41,270 --> 00:21:43,110
I'm Ko Gi Han's daughter,
Ko Eun Seol.

344
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:46,410
So please don't feel that way, okay?

345
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,980
It'll actually upset me.

346
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,680
Okay.

347
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:56,290
I hear you.

348
00:21:56,290 --> 00:21:58,420
I'll just focus on my own life
for a while.

349
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:01,960
So don't get too upset over it,
okay?

350
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:05,060
All right.

351
00:22:08,530 --> 00:22:11,300
For this Cheongrok Society meeting,
how much are you going to donate?

352
00:22:11,770 --> 00:22:14,300
We'll just stick
to the usual amount.

353
00:22:14,770 --> 00:22:16,640
Be more generous this time.

354
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:19,710
It seems Chairman Kim
is providing strong support.

355
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:22,410
Why go to such lengths?

356
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:25,450
We just need to do
as much as everyone else.

357
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:29,290
I'm telling you,
it's not just a simple donation.

358
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:32,890
It speaks to Cheongma's image,

359
00:22:33,490 --> 00:22:35,560
and it shows where we stand.

360
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:41,570
You seem to care too much
about what others think.

361
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:45,270
My father was never like that.

362
00:22:46,170 --> 00:22:47,640
Especially at gatherings like this,

363
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,840
whether it was wealth or ability,
he never showed it off.

364
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:55,250
My father always used to say,

365
00:22:56,050 --> 00:22:59,420
the deeper the ocean,
the calmer the waters.

366
00:23:01,450 --> 00:23:04,420
Showing off your donations
at these meetings?

367
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:06,260
It makes you look
incredibly shallow.

368
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:17,430
Come in.

369
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:26,610
Sir, I heard the Cheongrok Society
is meeting today.

370
00:23:27,580 --> 00:23:29,650
This is a custom-made tie pin
I prepared in advance.

371
00:23:30,850 --> 00:23:34,180
I know that Chairman Kim has
a great eye for accessories.

372
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:36,020
This will get noticed.

373
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,220
Thank you.

374
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:40,890
Hae Ra's mother...

375
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:43,460
is quite oblivious
when it comes to things like this.

376
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:46,900
Anyway,

377
00:23:48,570 --> 00:23:51,070
did you look into something
we could give to Chairman Kim?

378
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,900
I ordered a tea set...

379
00:23:53,970 --> 00:23:55,370
from Chairman Kim's
favorite tea house.

380
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,440
Good job.

381
00:23:57,610 --> 00:23:59,780
You always get things done.

382
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:03,950
Chairman Kim is a key figure
in this industry...

383
00:24:05,220 --> 00:24:07,720
who controls the licensing
for the distribution networks.

384
00:24:08,690 --> 00:24:09,950
At this meeting,

385
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:13,520
we need to make it absolutely clear
that we are on Chairman Kim's side.

386
00:24:17,590 --> 00:24:19,000
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

387
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,030
You didn't forget our plans
with my mom, right?

388
00:24:22,430 --> 00:24:23,470
Of course not.

389
00:24:23,830 --> 00:24:25,570
Is she meeting us at the cafe?

390
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,700
Yes. I'll get there first,
so take your time.

391
00:24:28,610 --> 00:24:30,040
Okay, I'll see you later.

392
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:31,880
Ko Eun Seol.

393
00:24:34,780 --> 00:24:35,780
Thank you.

394
00:24:36,950 --> 00:24:39,680
Go on ahead and draw
with your mother.

395
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:41,620
I'll be checking your work.

396
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:51,960
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

397
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:55,330
You're right. She's getting to me.

398
00:24:58,700 --> 00:24:59,770
Ko Eun Seol.

399
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,910
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

400
00:25:15,990 --> 00:25:18,220
The new store's
interior design proposal.

401
00:25:18,290 --> 00:25:20,120
I think you should handle it.

402
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:21,990
Have it finished by tomorrow.

403
00:25:22,530 --> 00:25:23,590
Me?

404
00:25:24,230 --> 00:25:26,600
I need to turn in
the factory inspection report today.

405
00:25:27,230 --> 00:25:28,900
Why? Can't you do it?

406
00:25:30,030 --> 00:25:31,700
Saying you can't do it
without even trying...

407
00:25:31,770 --> 00:25:33,240
is a clear neglect of duty.

408
00:25:33,670 --> 00:25:36,770
If managing workload
and physical limits...

409
00:25:36,770 --> 00:25:38,140
is part of your job,

410
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,880
then you're failing
to do yours, too.

411
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:42,610
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

412
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,120
The interior design proposal?

413
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:49,320
Have that completely finished
by today as well.

414
00:25:55,330 --> 00:25:56,360
Welcome...

415
00:25:57,290 --> 00:25:59,060
- Hi.
- Hey, guys.

416
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:03,300
I can't believe you didn't tell us
you opened a cafe.

417
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:06,240
Exactly. If we'd known,
we would've gotten you something.

418
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:08,470
Oh, come on.
There's no need for that.

419
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:12,240
Instead of a useless gift,
boosting sales is way better, right?

420
00:26:12,310 --> 00:26:13,680
Right. That's true.

421
00:26:14,180 --> 00:26:15,480
Care for a drink?

422
00:26:15,950 --> 00:26:17,080
Why not?

423
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:20,780
The mangoes that came in today
are super fresh.

424
00:26:21,050 --> 00:26:22,490
How about some mango juice?

425
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:24,690
I'm not really into sweet beverages.

426
00:26:25,890 --> 00:26:27,560
I'll have an iced Americano.
What about you?

427
00:26:28,330 --> 00:26:31,030
- Same here.
- How about some buns?

428
00:26:31,030 --> 00:26:32,800
No, thank you. I just ate.

429
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:34,660
Me too.

430
00:26:35,770 --> 00:26:38,370
Okay. Two iced Americanos?

431
00:26:38,370 --> 00:26:40,570
Yes. Should we sit over there?

432
00:26:42,670 --> 00:26:44,910
- It's pretty.
- Hold on a second.

433
00:26:45,710 --> 00:26:46,980
The cafe is a bit small.

434
00:26:48,310 --> 00:26:50,980
- It sure is.
- It's a little small, right?

435
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:55,220
(Americano Special Discount:
2 dollars)

436
00:26:57,250 --> 00:26:59,360
What was all that
about boosting sales?

437
00:26:59,420 --> 00:27:01,190
How much revenue
does a place like this make?

438
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:03,090
It wouldn't be much.

439
00:27:03,490 --> 00:27:05,700
I bet she can barely cover the rent.

440
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:08,630
- Right?
- I still have some left over.

441
00:27:08,630 --> 00:27:12,600
Running a place like this alone
as a woman can't be easy.

442
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:13,940
Of course.

443
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:15,970
There are so many
terrible customers these days.

444
00:27:16,170 --> 00:27:18,070
It's been tough for you, hasn't it?

445
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:20,280
I suppose so.

446
00:27:21,210 --> 00:27:24,850
That's why, like it or not,
having a husband is still the best.

447
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:27,620
Even for opening
a small cafe like this,

448
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:29,720
it feels a bit nerve-wracking
not having a husband around.

449
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:33,060
Right. Whenever I try
to do something,

450
00:27:33,120 --> 00:27:35,130
- I get really scared.
- Exactly.

451
00:27:35,130 --> 00:27:38,290
Hold on. Won't your kids
be getting home soon?

452
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,130
We still have plenty of time.

453
00:27:42,300 --> 00:27:45,800
By the way,
aren't you seeing anyone lately?

454
00:27:46,770 --> 00:27:48,140
Did you have to ask that?

455
00:27:49,010 --> 00:27:51,010
Where would she find a man?

456
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:54,440
She's probably too busy trying
to provide for herself and her son.

457
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,850
Really, a man?

458
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,620
Right here. I'm her man.

459
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:03,920
Oh, gosh.

460
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:06,220
Baby, are they your close friends?

461
00:28:07,490 --> 00:28:08,530
Yes.

462
00:28:09,190 --> 00:28:11,560
Then you should have
introduced me to them.

463
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:13,800
Sorry for the late introduction.

464
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:16,600
I'm Ko Eun Guk, Mi Rae's boyfriend.

465
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,670
- I see.
- Oh, right.

466
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:22,340
Mi Rae kept telling me
we shouldn't go public yet,

467
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:24,570
but since you guys
are so close to her...

468
00:28:25,710 --> 00:28:26,710
It's okay, right?

469
00:28:29,350 --> 00:28:31,650
Baby, you must be too warm.

470
00:28:31,850 --> 00:28:33,750
Why are you sweating so much?

471
00:28:36,220 --> 00:28:37,890
She usually runs cold,

472
00:28:38,190 --> 00:28:39,360
but ever since we got together,

473
00:28:39,420 --> 00:28:41,220
she's been feeling the heat
a lot more.

474
00:28:42,290 --> 00:28:44,230
Baby, are you okay?

475
00:28:44,390 --> 00:28:45,460
I'm fine.

476
00:28:47,930 --> 00:28:50,230
- Here.
- Thank you.

477
00:28:50,230 --> 00:28:56,610
(24th Cheongrok Society Dinner)

478
00:28:57,410 --> 00:29:00,910
I heard Cheongma's new brand
is getting a great response lately.

479
00:29:02,050 --> 00:29:04,410
Word is, the person in charge
is a talent from...

480
00:29:04,410 --> 00:29:05,520
the group's scholarship foundation.

481
00:29:05,750 --> 00:29:07,050
That's correct, Chairman Kim.

482
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:09,350
A young friend started the brand,

483
00:29:09,350 --> 00:29:11,490
and it's been solid
right from the get-go.

484
00:29:12,990 --> 00:29:14,760
It's all thanks
to the Chairman's late father,

485
00:29:15,130 --> 00:29:18,290
who built a strong foundation
for the foundation early on.

486
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:20,400
Thank you for saying so.

487
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:23,430
The foundation nurtures talent,

488
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:26,940
and those people become
a reliable future for Cheongma.

489
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:32,040
It's not merely a business,
but a true enterprise.

490
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:34,810
Thank you
for thinking so highly of it.

491
00:29:36,380 --> 00:29:38,010
Chairman, Ma'am.

492
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:39,750
Cheers.

493
00:29:46,290 --> 00:29:47,390
(24th Cheongrok Society Dinner)

494
00:29:48,220 --> 00:29:49,230
Excuse me, sir.

495
00:29:50,190 --> 00:29:55,600
This is a custom tea set
from the tea house you go to often.

496
00:29:56,830 --> 00:30:00,440
Why are you giving me this
here and now?

497
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:02,410
Honey.

498
00:30:04,470 --> 00:30:06,940
Please don't read too much into it.

499
00:30:06,940 --> 00:30:09,580
To secure
Cheongma's distribution network,

500
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,250
I was hoping I'd...

501
00:30:11,250 --> 00:30:14,120
What do you think
this gathering is for?

502
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:16,990
We might be business people,

503
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:19,920
but inside the Cheongrok Society,

504
00:30:20,290 --> 00:30:22,630
we leave personal gain at the door.

505
00:30:23,190 --> 00:30:26,460
It was Chairman Kim's late father
who first honored that vision.

506
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:29,470
If we forget our core values
and start exchanging favors like this,

507
00:30:29,930 --> 00:30:33,040
what is this gathering
other than a place for bribery?

508
00:30:35,710 --> 00:30:38,680
This is why you can't ignore
where a person comes from.

509
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:45,280
Sir.

510
00:30:46,050 --> 00:30:47,880
Oh, no. Sir?

511
00:30:58,700 --> 00:31:01,330
For the time being,
don't contact Chairman Kim.

512
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:03,930
I'll offer him a sincere apology.

513
00:31:04,270 --> 00:31:05,700
You should stay out of it.

514
00:31:05,940 --> 00:31:09,540
You don't know
how to handle these situations.

515
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:11,310
Please just listen to me.

516
00:31:12,740 --> 00:31:14,640
What don't I know?

517
00:31:15,210 --> 00:31:16,980
Are you judging people
by their backgrounds...

518
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:18,150
and sorting them into classes, too?

519
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:19,750
What?

520
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:23,320
Why are you being so twisted?

521
00:31:23,750 --> 00:31:25,990
How are you and I
in different classes?

522
00:31:26,260 --> 00:31:28,120
And who decides
those classes anyway?

523
00:31:28,590 --> 00:31:30,130
Seriously, what is wrong with you?

524
00:31:30,130 --> 00:31:31,890
Forget it. Just stop.

525
00:31:34,260 --> 00:31:35,270
Seriously!

526
00:31:36,570 --> 00:31:38,670
He's been driving me crazy all day.

527
00:31:54,820 --> 00:31:57,250
Sir, I thought you'd be asleep.

528
00:31:58,420 --> 00:32:01,390
I'll turn in
once I finish this drink.

529
00:32:02,690 --> 00:32:04,960
I heard about what happened
with Chairman Kim.

530
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:08,530
I'm sorry. I should've known better.

531
00:32:10,270 --> 00:32:12,700
How could I possibly
understand the minds...

532
00:32:13,170 --> 00:32:14,900
of those who are noble to the bone?

533
00:32:16,710 --> 00:32:20,110
They make dirty deals
behind closed doors,

534
00:32:20,580 --> 00:32:22,280
then act all classy in public.

535
00:32:24,980 --> 00:32:26,850
Born with silver spoons
in their mouths,

536
00:32:27,680 --> 00:32:30,890
they dress up their hypocrisy
as dignity.

537
00:32:33,390 --> 00:32:34,390
Wait.

538
00:32:39,230 --> 00:32:40,230
But...

539
00:32:41,700 --> 00:32:44,070
do you know what makes me
even more twisted?

540
00:32:45,840 --> 00:32:49,470
Jung Sun is the one
who deceives me the most.

541
00:32:50,810 --> 00:32:51,910
My own wife.

542
00:32:59,050 --> 00:33:02,050
Please stop.
You've had too much to drink.

543
00:33:03,750 --> 00:33:04,750
Let go.

544
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,600
What are you two doing?

545
00:33:48,970 --> 00:33:52,540
(A Trap Called Desire)

546
00:33:52,700 --> 00:33:54,540
No matter how handsome he is,

547
00:33:54,540 --> 00:33:56,340
my friend Hee Jung's daughter...

548
00:33:56,340 --> 00:33:58,210
would never go for a guy
with a fiancee.

549
00:33:58,410 --> 00:34:01,040
Couples with a big age gap
are the trend these days.

550
00:34:01,110 --> 00:34:03,410
- I'll be your eternal...
- Take a look at this.

551
00:34:03,410 --> 00:34:06,750
Just you wait.
Your mother has a plan.

552
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:08,220
Look here, Secretary Choi,

553
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:10,220
I don't think
you've grasped the situation yet.

554
00:34:10,390 --> 00:34:12,720
Have you not been told who I am yet?

555
00:34:12,720 --> 00:34:15,660
If it's for the CEO and Cheongma,
I'll do whatever it takes.

556
00:34:15,660 --> 00:34:17,230
You'll go crazy from the stress.

557
00:34:17,660 --> 00:34:19,500
It's going to be quite a show
from here on out.

558
00:34:19,530 --> 00:34:20,930
There's a girl named Ko Eun Seol.

559
00:34:20,930 --> 00:34:23,730
Right now, she's the main person
we need to keep an eye on.

560
00:34:24,400 --> 00:34:25,400
Are you up for the task?

561
00:34:26,640 --> 00:34:28,640
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
